WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:06.525
Lab 1 runs on a laptop in the examples
folder, against fixtures, with no tenant.

3
00:00:06.525 --> 00:00:10.711
Ask for a cloud name the client
doesn't know, G C C High with capitals,

4
00:00:10.711 --> 00:00:14.587
and you get a value error that
lists the four names it accepts.

5
00:00:14.587 --> 00:00:17.626
An unknown name is an
error, never a default.

6
00:00:17.626 --> 00:00:22.766
List the permissions the stale-users task
needs, and you get exactly two: AuditLog

7
00:00:22.766 --> 00:00:27.600
dot Read dot All and User dot Read dot
All, computed from the calls it declares.

8
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.803
Make a call the Conditional Access
task doesn't declare, and it refuses,

9
00:00:31.803 --> 00:00:35.788
telling you to add it to graph-calls
dot JSON with its permission.

10
00:00:35.788 --> 00:00:41.525
Send a GCC High token to the worldwide
Graph host, and it refuses again.

11
00:00:41.525 --> 00:00:43.412
Nothing was sent in either case.

12
00:00:43.412 --> 00:00:46.750
Then nine tests prove
paging, retries, batching,

13
00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:51.113
delta and the advanced-query
header against a fake transport.

14
00:00:51.113 --> 00:00:55.418
The lab repeats the rules in
PowerShell, and the full suites pass:

15
00:00:55.418 --> 00:00:58.320
seventy in pytest and
forty-four in Pester.
